* text=auto eol=lf
# A case's own input files are bytes, not text: what a case hands a program.
# The rule above rewrites CR LF to LF when a text file is committed, so Rush
# 02's crlf.dict, whose line endings ARE its case, reached every clone with
# LF only -- the case tested nothing and ex00_oracle_fixtures failed there,
# while the checkout that wrote it was green. Only an exercise's fixtures/
# folder is exempt: a file whose CRs are its case goes there, and a CR in a
# clue, a script or an expected output beside it is an editor's, which the
# rule above strips. //tools:conventions refuses a file the rule above would
# rewrite (a CR LF, and no lone CR, which makes git keep the file as it is)
# that no -text or binary rule here covers, and a CR in a harness text file
# (a clues*.tsv, a script, a BUILD or .bzl file) even where one does.
**/tests/ex[0-9][0-9]/fixtures/** -text
